   "text": "The structure is DTPA-conjugated octreotide (pentetreotide). Its parts are a DTPA chelator acylating the N-terminus of D-Phe, then the cyclic peptide Cys\u2013Phe\u2013D-Trp\u2013Lys\u2013Thr\u2013Cys with a disulfide bridge, and a C-terminal threoninol.\n\nI assigned the stereochemistry from the standard octreotide configuration (L-Cys, L-Phe, D-Trp, L-Lys, L-Thr, L-Cys, L-threoninol, D-Phe at the N-terminus). I did not check each wedge and hash in the drawing individually against this.\n\nReading from the left:\n1. DTPA: three N atoms joined by two ethylene links, carrying five CH2COOH arms. The fifth arm is the amide carbonyl, CH2C(=O)\u2013, attached to D-Phe.\n2. D-Phe, with its benzyl side chain.\n3. Cys, whose CH2\u2013S forms the disulfide to the second Cys.\n4. L-Phe.\n5. D-Trp, with its indole side chain.\n6. L-Lys, with its (CH2)4NH2 side chain.\n7. L-Thr.\n8. Cys, closing the disulfide ring through the S\u2013S bond.\n9. Threoninol, ending in CH2OH and CH(CH3)OH.\n\nI wrote the disulfide as ring-closure label %10 on the two sulfur atoms.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CC(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc4ccccc4)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc4c[nH]c5ccccc45)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)CO"
